WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.976 --> 00:00:18.267
People near the courtroom doors began to sneeze.

2
00:00:18.287 --> 00:00:21.949
"I know who the next witness is!"

3
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:22.890
Alice said.

4
00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.112
"It must be the Duchess' cook."

5
00:00:26.513 --> 00:00:27.473
Alice was correct.

6
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:31.316
The Cook entered the courtroom, carrying her pepper shaker.

7
00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:34.886
"Tell us your story!"

8
00:00:35.406 --> 00:00:36.327
the King commanded.

9
00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:39.570
"No, I refuse!"

10
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.711
The Cook crossed her arms.

11
00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:44.474
The King didn't know what to do.

12
00:00:45.855 --> 00:00:47.876
He looked at the White Rabbit for advice.

13
00:00:49.778 --> 00:00:55.602
"Your Majesty, you must get this witness to tell her story," the White Rabbit said.

14
00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:59.866
"The Knave of Hearts is accused of stealing the Queen's tarts.

15
00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.208
This woman is a cook.

16
00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:04.965
She knows all about tarts."

17
00:01:06.786 --> 00:01:11.948
"Well, if I must, then I must," the King said.

18
00:01:13.068 --> 00:01:15.909
Then he frowned at the Cook for a long time.

19
00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:21.272
Finally he said, "What are tarts made of?"

20
00:01:21.292 --> 00:01:25.293
"Mostly pepper," the Cook said.

21
00:01:30.235 --> 00:01:31.896
said a sleepy voice behind her.

22
00:01:33.357 --> 00:01:35.338
"Seize that Dormouse!"

23
00:01:35.778 --> 00:01:36.619
the Queen shrieked.

24
00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:39.641
"Remove that Dormouse from court!

25
00:01:40.441 --> 00:01:41.422
Off with his head!

26
00:01:42.002 --> 00:01:43.564
Off with his whiskers!"

27
00:01:46.766 --> 00:01:52.269
For a few minutes, the whole courtroom was in confusion as the Dormouse was removed.

28
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.373
By the time everyone settled down again, the Cook had disappeared.

29
00:01:57.393 --> 00:02:01.536
"Forget about the Cook."

30
00:02:02.496 --> 00:02:06.438
The King sounded relieved that he didn't have to deal with her anymore.

31
00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:10.681
"Really, my dear," he whispered to the Queen.

32
00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:14.423
"You must question the next witness.

33
00:02:15.324 --> 00:02:19.506
Dealing with all these people is making my head hurt."

34
00:02:20.627 --> 00:02:23.789
"No, it's your job," the Queen said firmly.

35
00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.512
Alice watched the White Rabbit hold up his scroll of paper.

36
00:02:29.464 --> 00:02:33.325
"They really don't have any evidence against the Knave of Hearts yet," she thought.

37
00:02:33.345 --> 00:02:36.086
"I wonder who the next witness will be."

38
00:02:36.106 --> 00:02:39.827
"Alice!" the White Rabbit called loudly.

39
00:02:40.987 --> 00:02:44.548
Alice jumped when she heard her name on the White Rabbit's scroll.

40
00:02:44.568 --> 00:02:50.010
"Here!" Alice leaped to her feet, forgetting how large she'd grown.

41
00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.411
She knocked over the jury box, and all the jurors tumbled out.

42
00:02:54.431 --> 00:02:57.132
"Oh, I'm so sorry!"

43
00:02:57.472 --> 00:02:58.092
Alice cried.

44
00:02:59.164 --> 00:03:02.085
Last week she'd knocked over a bowl of goldfish.

45
00:03:02.885 --> 00:03:04.666
This accident reminded her of that.

46
00:03:05.846 --> 00:03:09.907
She felt as if she had to put the jurors back quickly, or they'd die.

47
00:03:12.508 --> 00:03:14.208
The King scowled at Alice.

48
00:03:14.228 --> 00:03:21.810
"This trial cannot go on until the jurors are back in their proper places."

49
00:03:25.712 --> 00:03:27.132
Alice began working on it.

50
00:03:29.228 --> 00:03:32.829
But then she realized she'd put a lizard in upside down.

51
00:03:33.789 --> 00:03:35.430
She put the creature right side up.

52
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:39.811
"Putting the jurors back is actually very silly," Alice thought.

53
00:03:39.831 --> 00:03:42.992
"None of these creatures will be much help at this trial."

54
00:03:44.913 --> 00:03:47.414
The jurors' slates were found and returned to them.

55
00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:50.895
They all began to write about the accident.

56
00:03:51.795 --> 00:03:54.656
All except the lizard, who stared at the ceiling.

57
00:03:56.188 --> 00:03:59.991
"What do you know about this tart business?"

58
00:04:00.511 --> 00:04:01.672
the King asked Alice.

59
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:04.334
"Nothing," Alice replied.

60
00:04:04.354 --> 00:04:06.736
"Nothing at all?"

61
00:04:07.196 --> 00:04:07.997
the King asked.

62
00:04:08.977 --> 00:04:10.899
"Nothing at all," she repeated.

63
00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.862
For a few minutes, the jurors kept writing on their slates.

64
00:04:17.904 --> 00:04:19.385
The King wrote in a notebook.

65
00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:23.668
Suddenly he called out, "Silence!"

66
00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.905
even though no one was talking.

67
00:04:28.006 --> 00:04:29.726
He read aloud from his notebook.

68
00:04:30.787 --> 00:04:38.010
"'Rule 42: All people more than a mile high must leave the courtroom.'"

69
00:04:40.851 --> 00:04:42.311
Everyone stared at Alice.

70
00:04:43.152 --> 00:04:44.552
"I'm not a mile high."

71
00:04:44.572 --> 00:04:49.114
"Yes, you are," the King said.

72
00:04:49.134 --> 00:04:53.416
"Almost two miles high," the Queen added.

73
00:04:54.688 --> 00:04:56.729
"Well, I'm not leaving," Alice said.

74
00:04:56.749 --> 00:05:00.470
"Besides, that's not a real rule; you just made it up."

75
00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:06.112
"It's the oldest rule in the book," the King said.

76
00:05:06.132 --> 00:05:10.413
"Then it should be Rule One," Alice replied.

77
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:12.894
The King shook with anger.

78
00:05:18.335 --> 00:05:20.136
what is your verdict?"
